# ☸️ Design a Multi-Tenant EKS Cluster with Isolation Across Dev, QA, and Prod

## Objective

Provide strong isolation between:

* Dev
* QA
* Production

while preventing:

* noisy neighbors
* security leakage
* resource starvation

---

# 🏗️ Recommended Architecture

```text id="2v3vyo"
                    AWS Organization
                            │
                            ▼
                         EKS Cluster
        ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
        │                                     │
        ▼                                     ▼
   Shared Services                    Tenant Workloads
        │                                     │
        ├── Monitoring                        ├── Dev Namespace
        ├── Logging                           ├── QA Namespace
        ├── Ingress                           └── Prod Namespace
        └── Security
```

---

# 🔐 Isolation Strategy

## 1. Namespace Isolation

Separate namespaces:

```text id="m0t7a5"
dev
qa
prod
```

---

## 2. RBAC

Environment-specific IAM + RBAC.

Example:

* Dev team cannot access prod namespace
* Read-only QA access
* Admin-only production access

---

## 3. Network Policies

Prevent pod communication across environments.

Example:

```text id="w93qug"
Dev pods CANNOT talk to Prod pods
```

Use:

* Calico
* Cilium

---

## 4. Dedicated Node Groups

| Environment | Dedicated Nodes           |
| ----------- | ------------------------- |
| Dev         | Spot instances            |
| QA          | Shared nodes              |
| Prod        | Dedicated On-Demand nodes |

Use:

* taints/tolerations
* node affinity

to isolate workloads.

---

## 5. Resource Quotas & Limits

Prevent noisy neighbors.

Use:

* ResourceQuota
* LimitRange
* requests/limits

Example:

```yaml id="wn0q8e"
resources:
  requests:
    cpu: "500m"
    memory: "1Gi"
```

---

## 6. Pod Security

Enforce:

* restricted PSP/PSS
* non-root containers
* read-only filesystem
* seccomp profiles

